          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/bb84842234f70446459edd1a0d63422ee29d5111"
        }
      ],
      "message": "rpc: Support different types for param aliases\n\nAn RPC parameter can have aliases but only one type. Let it declare a\ntype per alias, so that one position can take a new options object\nunder one name and the old boolean under another. Replacing positional\nparameters with an options object without breaking existing callers\nneeds this.\n\nMatchesType accepts any of the declared types, and GetArgMap lists each\nalias with its own type, so the client conversion table is checked per\nname.\n\nCo-authored-by: jeanpablojp <me@jeanpablo.jp>",
      "committer": {
        "name": "jeanpablo",
        "email": "me@jeanpablo.jp",
        "date": "2026-11-25T17:24:07Z"
