        }
      ],
      "message": "rpc: Keep mixed positional and named calls working\n\nA named-only option that a positional parameter also accepts by name\n(also_positional) always goes into the options object. When positional\narguments passed in \"args\" already take the position of that object,\nthe call fails with \"specified twice\", although the option could go to\nthe positional parameter of the same name. Pass it there instead.\n\nNo RPC has this layout yet. The next commit gives walletprocesspsbt\none, and without this change a call such as\n`walletprocesspsbt <psbt> true finalize=false` with -named, which works\ntoday, would start to fail.",
