      ],
      "message": "rpc, wallet: Convert walletprocesspsbt to options\n\nMove sign, sighashtype, bip32derivs and finalize into an options object\nas the second parameter, so that new settings do not have to become\nmore positional parameters.\n\nExisting calls keep working. The second position still accepts the sign\nboolean, sighashtype, bip32derivs and finalize stay as hidden positional\nparameters, and all four can still be passed by name. A null option\nmeans the default, as a null named argument did before.\n\nThe options are read before waiting for the wallet to sync and decoding\nthe PSBT, so invalid options are reported first. The conversion check\nin rpc_help.py compares sets now, because sign is listed at position 1\nboth as an option and as an alias.\n\nCo-authored-by: jeanpablojp <me@jeanpablo.jp>",
      "committer": {
        "name": "jeanpablo",
        "email": "me@jeanpablo.jp",
        "date": "2026-11-25T17:24:07Z"
