      ],
      "message": "rpc: Enforce the declared type of named params\n\nA parameter passed by name must have the type declared for that name,\nso walletprocesspsbt rejects options=true instead of reading it as\nsign=true. A parameter passed by position can still have any of its\ndeclared types.\n\ntransformNamedArguments records the name each parameter was passed\nunder. Holes and an options object built from named options get no\nname, so the parameters after them keep their own.\n\nCo-authored-by: jeanpablojp <me@jeanpablo.jp>",
